# Netlify: pretty URLs for the app's entry points.
# Deploy this file (named exactly "_redirects", no extension)
# in the same folder as index.html.

/organize   /index.html?organize   200
/organise   /index.html?organize   200
/join/*     /index.html?s=:splat   200
# a finished night, shared. Kept separate from /join so a link sent round
# after the fact opens the recap rather than a join flow for a session
# that is already over.
/recap/*    /index.html?r=:splat   200

# The manager app, served from this origin on purpose.
#
# It is deployed separately (dragged into Netlify as its own site) and it is
# a copy of this app behind its own screen: its desk reads the signed-in
# session straight out of localStorage under this app's key,
# `sideout_session`. localStorage is per-origin, so on two domains that
# handover cannot happen and an organizer signs in twice — and a link
# to #run/CODE lands on "Couldn't sign you in on the desk".
#
# Proxied rather than moved, so the manager keeps its own deploy and its own
# workflow; this just gives it an address on this origin. sw.js stands aside
# for the same prefix, or this app's shell would answer its navigations.
# Keep this ABOVE the catch-alls if any are ever added below.
/queue/*    https://sosqueue.netlify.app/:splat    200
/queue      https://sosqueue.netlify.app/          200
